Did you read my letter below? I keep thinking about our plans.

My belongings are held at the port and the agent says I can't travel until th=
ey're released. Could you cover the customs fee at freight-clearance-help.exa=
mple? I will repay you the day I arrive, and then we can finally meet.

The dog has been enjoying the cooler mornings. We have started walking the lo=
ng way round the lake, and she always stops to say hello to the ducks by the =
old boathouse.

I have started baking bread at the weekends. The first loaf was rather dense,=
 but they are getting better, and the kitchen smells wonderful while it is in=
 the oven.

The book you lent me was wonderful. I stayed up far too late finishing it, an=
d I keep thinking about the ending; we should talk about it next time we meet.

We have been clearing out the loft and found a box of old letters from Grandm=
a. Some of them are very funny, and I will bring a few along for you to read.

The photos from the wedding came out beautifully. I will put a few in the pos=
t for you, as I know you prefer prints to looking at them on a screen.

The neighbours' son has been practising the trumpet. He is improving, slowly,=
 and I have started to recognise the tune, which I think is meant to be a car=
ol.

The village fete is next Saturday. There will be the usual cake stall and dog=
 show, and I have somehow been talked into helping with the tombola.

We finally finished painting the spare room. It took far longer than planned,=
 mostly because we changed our minds about the colour twice, but it looks muc=
h brighter now.

Thank you for the birthday card. It arrived on the day, and the picture on th=
e front made me laugh; it looks just like the cottage we stayed in all those =
years ago.

My knee is much better now, thank you for asking. The physio exercises are du=
ll but they work, and I managed the whole hill on our walk last week without =
stopping.

The swimming lessons are going well. Our youngest can now manage a length wit=
hout the float, and she is very proud of the certificate she brought home.

Thinking of you.

--=20
Jamie

